Subject: [PATCH 11287/11362] Record the operator's answer on level-up-resolved
 cells: count all solved levels

The question was whether a level the classical path clears anyway counts as a
new-arm specification. Level 0 runs every arm dry then levels up regardless, and
the shadow control reached the same level-up pulling no lever. Operator answer:
count all solved levels.

This confirms the shipped behaviour rather than changing it, which is exactly why
it needed writing down. level_resolved_by_levelup is recorded and printed but read
by no filter anywhere in python/ or scripts/, so no code change follows. Recorded
so a future reader who notices an unused field does not add the filter as a
tightening -- dropping level-up-resolved cells would silently discard the only
cells the corpus currently produces.

